From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:38:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] patch 4: controller-side DPP Configurator task

Add the controller-side DPP Configurator FSM and its supporting crypto/key
storage:

- dpp_crypto_helper.{h,cpp} (new, controller-local): OpenSSL EC/ECDH/JWK
  helper plus json-c based JWK parsing.
- dpp_key_store.{h,cpp} (new): persists/loads DPP configurator keys.
- dpp_configurator_task.{h,cpp} (new): drives DPP Authentication/
  Configuration/Peer Discovery, wired chirp handling, and BSS Config
  Response TLV construction; calls BrokerClient::install_security_key()
  after the EAPOL 4-way handshake completes.
- controller.h/.cpp: registers DppConfiguratorTask in the task pool,
  dispatches DPP-related 1905 messages to it, and applies pending DPP
  radio info.
- db/agent.h, db/db.h: new per-agent fields (dpp_security_required,
  pmk_1905, tk_1905_installed, dpp_deferred_task_executed) and bootstrap
  hash storage, consumed by son_actions.cpp (blocks non-exception CMDUs to
  DPP agents before TK install; reports real 1905 security state in Agent
  List) and agent_monitoring_task.cpp (triggers the deferred task for DPP
  agents, which have no WSC M1 to normally trigger it).
- controller_ucc_listener.cpp: computes the bootstrap hash from the UCC
  supplied enrollee public key.

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
